  "id": "Compound::DB01126 - Gene::6716",
  "verbalization": "Dutasteride is likely to interact with Srd5a2 through a shared interaction with Srd5a1, as evidenced by multiple paths showing that Dutasteride binds to Srd5a1 and that Srd5a1 participates in steroid dehydrogenase activities, which are also participated by Srd5a2. These findings suggest a potential functional link between Dutasteride and Srd5a2, possibly through a common pathway involving steroid metabolism. The evidence supports a mechanism where Dutasteride may modulate Srd5a2 by influencing Srd5a1, which in turn affects steroid dehydrogenase activity. The consistent binding of Dutasteride to Srd5a1 across different paths reinforces the likelihood of a direct or indirect interaction with Srd5a2, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
